---
title: 'Quadrant Charts'
description: 'Divide a $framework Quadrant Chart into four labelled, independently styled regions around a pivot point.'
enterprise: true
---

A Quadrant Chart displays scatter or bubble data divided into four regions.

## Simple Quadrant Chart

{% chartExampleRunner title="Simple Quadrant Chart" name="simple-quadrant-chart" type="generated" /%}

The Quadrant Chart is designed to display a single series and is created using the `createQuadrantChart()` factory.
Options are supplied as a flat object, with no `series` or `axes` keys.

{% if isFramework("javascript") %}

```js
const options = {
    data: getData(),
    xKey: 'revenueGrowth',
    yKey: 'marginChange',
};

AgCharts.createQuadrantChart(options);
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("react") %}

```jsx format="reactHooks"
const [options, setOptions] = useState({
    data: getData(),
    xKey: 'revenueGrowth',
    yKey: 'marginChange',
});

return <AgQuadrantChart options={options} />;
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("angular") %}

```ts
@Component({
    selector: 'app-root',
    standalone: true,
    imports: [AgQuadrantChart],
    template: `<ag-quadrant-chart [options]="options"></ag-quadrant-chart>`,
})
export class AppComponent {
    public options: AgQuadrantChartOptions;
    constructor() {
        this.options = {
            data: getData(),
            xKey: 'revenueGrowth',
            yKey: 'marginChange',
        };
    }
}
```

{% /if %}

{% if isFramework("vue") %}

```js format="snippet"
template: `<ag-quadrant-chart :options="options" />`,
components: {
    'ag-quadrant-chart': AgQuadrantChart,
},
data() {
    return {
        options: {
            data: getData(),
            xKey: 'revenueGrowth',
            yKey: 'marginChange',
        },
    };
}
```

{% /if %}

In this configuration:

- `xKey` and `yKey` map the two measures being compared.

## Pivot

The `pivot` sets the data values at which the regions are divided.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Pivot" name="quadrant-chart-pivot" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    pivot: { x: 4, y: 6 },
}
```

In this configuration:

- `pivot.x` and `pivot.y` divide the chart into regions at an effort of `4` and an impact of `6`.
- The pivot is a data value rather than a proportion of the chart, so the four regions are not equally sized.

By default the axis lines move to cross at the pivot, while the axis titles and labels stay at the edge of the chart.

## Regions

Each of the four regions is configured under its own key in `regions`.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Regions" name="quadrant-chart-regions" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    regions: {
        label: { position: 'inside-outer-outer', spacing: 10 },
        topLeft: { label: { text: 'Shrinking, Wider Margins' } },
        topRight: { label: { text: 'Growing, Wider Margins' } },
        bottomLeft: { label: { text: 'Shrinking, Thinner Margins' } },
        bottomRight: { label: { text: 'Growing, Thinner Margins' } },
    },
}
```

In this example:

- Use `label.position` to move a region label to any corner or edge of the region, relative to the pivot.
- Use `label.spacing` to set the gap in pixels between a label and the region edges its `position` places it against.
  It defaults to `10`.

## Axes

`xAxis` and `yAxis` accept number axis options. Axis ticks are hidden by default.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Axes" name="quadrant-chart-axes" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    alignAxesToPivot: false,
    xAxis: {
        title: { text: 'Effort' },
        tick: { enabled: true },
    },
    yAxis: {
        title: { text: 'Impact' },
        tick: { enabled: true },
    },
}
```

In this configuration:

- `tick.enabled` shows the axis ticks, which are hidden by default.
- `alignAxesToPivot: false` holds the axes at their usual bottom and left positions rather than moving them to cross
  at the pivot. The regions are still divided at the pivot.

The axis line is drawn in a stronger colour than a standard axis, so it reads as a divider between regions rather
than as a chart edge. Override `xAxis.line` or `yAxis.line` to change its width or `stroke`.

See [Number Axis](./axes-types/#number) for the full range of axis options.

## Markers

Points are drawn as markers sized by `size`. Supplying `sizeKey` instead scales each marker by a third measure,
between `minSize` and `maxSize`.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Marker Sizes" name="quadrant-chart-size" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    sizeKey: 'revenue',
    minSize: 8,
    maxSize: 40,
}
```

In this configuration:

- `sizeKey` maps the data field controlling marker size.
- `minSize` and `maxSize` bound the size scale. `minSize` defaults to `size` when not set.

Marker text comes from `labelKey` and is styled and positioned with `label`. Labels are shown by default when
`labelKey` or a `label` object is set, and are otherwise hidden; set `label.enabled` to override either way. See
[Series Labels](./series-labels/) for label placement and collision options, and [Series Markers](./markers/) for
the available marker shapes.

## Tooltips

Hovering a marker shows the `xName`, `yName` and `labelName` values for that point. Use `tooltip.renderer` for full
control over the content.

See [Tooltips](./tooltips/) for more details.

## Customisation

### Regions

{% chartExampleRunner title="Region Styling" name="quadrant-chart-region-styling" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    regions: {
        topLeft: {
            fill: {
                type: 'gradient',
                rotation: 315,
                colorStops: [{ color: 'rgba(56, 189, 248, 0)' }, { color: '#38bdf8' }],
            },
            fillOpacity: 0.45,
            stroke: '#0284c7',
            strokeOpacity: 0.4,
            strokeWidth: 1,
            marker: { fill: '#38bdf8', strokeWidth: 0 },
            label: {
                text: 'Slower Warming, Wetter',
                color: '#0284c7',
                fontSize: 14,
                fontWeight: 'bold',
            },
        },
    },
}
```

In this configuration:

- `fill` takes a colour string or, as here, a gradient, pattern or image fill. `fillOpacity` fades it so the markers
  stay legible.
- `stroke`, `strokeOpacity` and `strokeWidth` outline the region.
- `marker` styles the points falling inside that region. Without it, points take the region's `fill` at full
  opacity, which is why an explicit `marker.fill` is needed alongside a gradient.
- `label` sets the region text and its font styling, which defaults to bold. Styling shared by every region goes on
  `regions.label`.

The remaining three regions follow the same shape, each with its own colour.

### Markers

Marker styles set at the top level apply to every point. The `itemStyler` callback overrides them per point, and
receives the `region` that point falls in.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Marker Styling" name="quadrant-chart-marker-styling" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    shape: 'circle',
    size: 12,
    strokeWidth: 2,
    itemStyler: ({ region }) => {
        switch (region) {
            case 'top-right':
                return { fill: '#16a34a', stroke: '#15803d', size: 18 };
            case 'top-left':
                return { fill: '#ca8a04', stroke: '#a16207' };
            case 'bottom-right':
                return { fill: '#2563eb', stroke: '#1d4ed8' };
            case 'bottom-left':
                return { fill: '#dc2626', stroke: '#b91c1c', shape: 'cross', strokeWidth: 3 };
        }
    },
}
```

In this configuration:

- `shape`, `size` and `strokeWidth` set the base style for all markers.
- `region` is `'top-left'`, `'top-right'`, `'bottom-left'` or `'bottom-right'`, letting each region's points be
  styled without repeating the pivot comparison. The callback also receives the `datum`, so styling can depend on
  the underlying values as well.
- Points in the top-right are enlarged and those in the bottom-left switch shape, so both regions stand out from the
  base style.

